<title>USA: OMI signs contracts with Daewoo.</title>
<headline>OMI signs contracts with Daewoo.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>OMI Corp said on Tuesday it awarded contracts to Daewoo Corp and Daewoo Heavy Industries for the construction of two Suezmax crude oil tankers of 156,000 dead weight tonnes each.</p>
<p>The vessels are scheduled to be delivered in the third and fourth quarters of 1998, the company said. OMI said it had an option for the construction of two additional Suexmaxes.</p>
<p>OMI also said it completed the acquisition of the Nordholm, a 30,000 dead weight tonne product courier built in 1991. Company officials were not immediately available to say from whom OMI bought the ship.</p>
</text>
